  "scope": [
    "Opt-in acyclic current array expansions use explicit SelectedElementTransfer records for both owned-place repacks and borrow-graph expansions.",
    "Split captures owner, logical index, target and entry model, then checks element and frame permissions and their value correspondence.",
    "Join captures current element and frame values, consumes the existing element/frame resources, and checks the recovered selected value and every other logical index.",
    "The matching owner/index frame predicate connects transitions; no inequality between physical element addresses is assumed.",
    "The existing opaque array split/join and generic caster contracts remain trusted translation. Their bodies and logical specifications are unchanged.",
    "Packages, saved-heap endpoints and cyclic bodies retain their prior encoding. Full continuation summaries and prophecy scope remain R2 work."
